    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_downward_heat_flux_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called \'surface\' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \'Water\' means water in all phases, including frozen i.e. ice and snow. \'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0298'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0299/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0299/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0299/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_downward_latent_heat_flux'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called \'surface\' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). The surface latent heat flux is the exchange of heat between the surface and the air on account of evaporation (including sublimation). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0299'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0301/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0301/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0301/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_downward_sensible_heat_flux'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called \'surface\' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). The surface sensible heat flux, also called \'turbulent\' heat flux, is the exchange of heat between the surface and the air by motion of air. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0301'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0302/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0302/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0302/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'surface_downward_water_flux'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The surface called \'surface\' means the lower boundary of the atmosphere. \'Water\' means water in all phases, including frozen i.e. ice and snow. \'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). The surface water flux is the result of precipitation and evaporation. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0302'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0305/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0305/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0305/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sound_intensity_level_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sound intensity is the sound energy per unit time per unit area. Sound intensity level in air is expressed on a logarithmic scale with reference to a sound intensity of 1e-12 W m-2. LI = 10 log10(I/I0) where LI is sound intensity level, I is sound intensity and I0 is the reference sound intensity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0305'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0306/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0306/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0306/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sound_intensity_level_in_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sound intensity is the sound energy per unit time per unit area. Sound intensity level in water is expressed on a logarithmic scale with reference to a sound intensity of 6.7e-19 W m-2. LI = 10 log10(I/I0) where LI is sound intensity level, I is sound intensity and I0 is the reference sound intensity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0306'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0307/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0307/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0307/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sound_pressure_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sound pressure is the difference from the local ambient pressure caused by a sound wave at a particular location and time.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0307'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0308/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0308/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0308/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sound_pressure_in_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sound pressure is the difference from the local ambient pressure caused by a sound wave at a particular location and time.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0308'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0309/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0309/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0309/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sound_pressure_level_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sound pressure is the difference from the local ambient pressure caused by a sound wave at a particular location and time. Sound pressure level in air is expressed on a logarithmic scale with reference to a sound pressure of 2e-5 Pa. Lp = 20 log10(p/p0) where Lp is the sound pressure level, p is the rms sound pressure and p0 is the reference sound pressure.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0309'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0310/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0310/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0310/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sound_pressure_level_in_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sound pressure is the difference from the local ambient pressure caused by a sound wave at a particular location and time. Sound pressure level in water is expressed on a logarithmic scale with reference to a sound pressure of 1e-6 Pa. Lp = 20 log10(p/p0) where Lp is the sound pressure level, p is the rms sound pressure and p0 is the reference sound pressure.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0310'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0311/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0311/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0311/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'specific_dry_energy_of_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'specific\' means per unit mass. Dry energy is the sum of dry static energy and kinetic energy. Dry static energy is the sum of enthalpy and potential energy (itself the sum of gravitational and centripetal potential energy). Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0311'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0312/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0312/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0312/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'specific_gravitational_potential_energy'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'specific\' means per unit mass. Potential energy is the sum of the gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the centripetal potential energy. (The geopotential is the specific potential energy.)'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0312'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0313/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0313/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0313/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'specific_humidity'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'specific\' means per unit mass. Specific humidity is the mass fraction of water vapor in (moist) air.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0313'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0314/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0314/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0314/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'specific_kinetic_energy_of_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'specific\' means per unit mass.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0314'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0315/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0315/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0315/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'speed_of_sound_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Speed is the magnitude of velocity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0315'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0316/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0316/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0316/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'speed_of_sound_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Speed is the magnitude of velocity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0316'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0319/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0319/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0319/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'square_of_eastward_wind'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'square_of_X\' means X*X. \'Eastward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name upward_air_velocity.)'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0319'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0320/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0320/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0320/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'square_of_geopotential_height'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'square_of_X\' means X*X. Geopotential is the sum of the specific gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the specific centripetal potential energy. Geopotential height is the geopotential divided by the standard acceleration due to gravity. It is numerically similar to the altitude (or geometric height) and not to the quantity with standard name height, which is relative to the surface.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0320'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0322/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0322/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0322/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'square_of_northward_wind'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'square_of_X\' means X*X. \'Northward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name upward_air_velocity.)'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0322'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0323/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0323/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0323/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'square_of_upward_air_velocity'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'square_of_X\' means X*X. A velocity is a vector quantity. \'Upward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward). Upward air velocity is the vertical component of the 3D air velocity vector.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0323'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0325/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0325/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0325/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'subsurface_runoff_amount'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Amount\' means mass per unit area. Runoff is the liquid water which drains from land. If not specified, \'runoff\' refers to the sum of surface runoff and subsurface drainage.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0325'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0326/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0326/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0326/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'subsurface_runoff_flux'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Runoff is the liquid water which drains from land. If not specified, \'runoff\' refers to the sum of surface runoff and subsurface drainage. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0326'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0334/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0334/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0334/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sea_water_speed'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Speed is the magnitude of velocity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0334'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0343/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0343/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0343/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'snowfall_amount'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Amount\' means mass per unit area.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0343'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0344/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0344/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0344/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'snowfall_flux'@en ;
    skos:definition 'In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0344'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0347/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0347/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0347/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'soil_frozen_water_content'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'frozen_water\' means ice. \'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. The \'soil content\' of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface down to the bottom of the soil model. For the content between specified levels in the soil, standard names including content_of_soil_layer are used.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0347'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0348/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0348/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0348/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'soil_hydraulic_conductivity_at_saturation'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Hydraulic conductivity is the constant k in Darcy\'s Law q=-k grad h for fluid flow q (volume transport per unit area i.e. velocity) through a porous medium, where h is the hydraulic head (pressure expressed as an equivalent depth of water).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0348'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0350/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0350/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0350/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'soil_moisture_content_at_field_capacity'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'moisture\' means water in all phases contained in soil. \'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. The \'soil content\' of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface down to the bottom of the soil model. For the content between specified levels in the soil, standard names including content_of_soil_layer are used. The field capacity of soil is the maximum content of water it can retain against gravitational drainage.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0350'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0351/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0351/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0351/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'soil_porosity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The soil porosity is the proportion of its total volume not occupied by soil solids.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0351'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0353/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0353/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0353/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'soil_suction_at_saturation'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Soil suction is the tensile stress on water in soil due to molecular forces acting at the water-soil particle boundary. The forces may cause water to be drawn into the spaces within the soil matrix or cause it to be held in the soil without draining. Soil suction occurs in soil above the water table.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0353'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0357/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0357/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0357/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'soil_type'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A variable with the standard name of soil_type contains strings which indicate the character of the soil e.g. clay. These strings have not yet been standardised. Alternatively, the data variable may contain integers which can be translated to strings using flag_values and flag_meanings attributes.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0357'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0358/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0358/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0358/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'solar_azimuth_angle'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Solar azimuth angle is the horizontal angle between the line of sight to the sun and a reference direction which is often due north. The angle is measured clockwise.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0358'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0359/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0359/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0359/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'solar_elevation_angle'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Solar elevation angle is the angle between the line of sight to the sun and the local horizontal.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0359'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0360/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0360/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0360/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'solar_zenith_angle'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Solar zenith angle is the the angle between the line of sight to the sun and the local vertical.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0360'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0361/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0361/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0361/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sound_frequency'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Frequency is the number of oscillations of a wave per unit time.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0361'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0362/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0362/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0362/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'sound_intensity_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Sound intensity is the sound energy per unit time per unit area.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0362'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0363/1/> .
