    skos:definition 'A velocity is a vector quantity. \'Northward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0494'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0496/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0496/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0496/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'net_rate_of_absorption_of_shortwave_energy_in_atmosphere_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'shortwave\' means shortwave radiation. \'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Net absorbed radiation is the difference between absorbed and emitted radiation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0496'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0497/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0497/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0497/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'net_upward_longwave_flux_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'longwave\' means longwave radiation. \'Upward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward). Net upward radiation is the difference between radiation from below (upwelling) and radiation from above (downwelling). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0497'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0498/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0498/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0498/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'net_upward_longwave_flux_in_air_assuming_clear_sky'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A phrase assuming_condition indicates that the named quantity is the value which would obtain if all aspects of the system were unaltered except for the assumption of the circumstances specified by the condition. \'longwave\' means longwave radiation. \'Upward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed upward (negative downward). Net upward radiation is the difference between radiation from below (upwelling) and radiation from above (downwelling). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0498'^^xsd:string .
