    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0524'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0526/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0526/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0526/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'net_rate_of_absorption_of_longwave_energy_in_atmosphere_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'longwave\' means longwave radiation. \'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Net absorbed radiation is the difference between absorbed and emitted radiation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0526'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0527/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0527/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0527/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_water_evaporation_rate'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'lwe\' means liquid water equivalent. \'Water\' means water in all phases. Evaporation is the conversion of liquid or solid into vapor. (The conversion of solid alone into vapor is called \'sublimation\'.)'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0527'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0529/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0529/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0529/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'mass_concentration_of_oxygen_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Mass concentration means mass per unit volume and is used in the construction mass_concentration_of_X_in_Y, where X is a material constituent of Y.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0529'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0549/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0549/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0549/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'model_level_number'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Model level number should be understood as equivalent to layer number.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0549'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0550/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0550/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0550/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'model_level_number_at_convective_cloud_base'@en ;
    skos:definition 'cloud_base refers to the base of the lowest cloud. Model level number should be understood as equivalent to layer number. Convective cloud is that produced by the convection schemes in an atmosphere model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0550'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0551/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0551/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0551/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'model_level_number_at_convective_cloud_top'@en ;
    skos:definition 'cloud_top refers to the top of the highest cloud. Model level number should be understood as equivalent to layer number. Convective cloud is that produced by the convection schemes in an atmosphere model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0551'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0552/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0552/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0552/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'model_level_number_at_top_of_atmosphere_boundary_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Model level number should be understood as equivalent to layer number.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0552'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0554/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0554/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0554/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'longitude'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Longitude is positive eastward; its units of degree_east (or equivalent) indicate this explicitly. In a latitude-longitude system defined with respect to a rotated North Pole, the standard name of grid_longitude should be used instead of longitude. Grid longitude is positive in the grid-eastward direction, but its units should be plain degree.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0554'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0556/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0556/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0556/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_convective_snowfall_rate'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'lwe\' means liquid water equivalent.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0556'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0560/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0560/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0560/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_snowfall_rate'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'lwe\' means liquid water equivalent.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0560'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0564/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0564/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0564/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_thickness_of_convective_snowfall_amount'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'lwe\' means liquid water equivalent. \'Amount\' means mass per unit area. The construction lwe_thickness_of_X_amount or _content means the vertical extent of a layer of liquid water having the same mass per unit area.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0564'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0565/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0565/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0565/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_thickness_of_frozen_water_content_of_soil_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'frozen_water\' means ice. \'lwe\' means liquid water equivalent. The construction lwe_thickness_of_X_amount or _content means the vertical extent of a layer of liquid water having the same mass per unit area. \'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. \'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Quantities defined for a soil layer must have a vertical coordinate variable with boundaries indicating the extent of the layer(s).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0565'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0568/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0568/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0568/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_thickness_of_moisture_content_of_soil_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'lwe\' means liquid water equivalent. \'moisture\' means water in all phases contained in soil. The construction lwe_thickness_of_X_amount or _content means the vertical extent of a layer of liquid water having the same mass per unit area. \'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. \'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Quantities defined for a soil layer must have a vertical coordinate variable with boundaries indicating the extent of the layer(s).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0568'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0570/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0570/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0570/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_thickness_of_snowfall_amount'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'lwe\' means liquid water equivalent. \'Amount\' means mass per unit area. The construction lwe_thickness_of_X_amount or _content means the vertical extent of a layer of liquid water having the same mass per unit area.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0570'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0571/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0571/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0571/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_thickness_of_soil_moisture_content'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'lwe\' means liquid water equivalent. \'moisture\' means water in all phases contained in soil. The construction lwe_thickness_of_X_amount or _content means the vertical extent of a layer of liquid water having the same mass per unit area. \'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. The \'soil content\' of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface down to the bottom of the soil model. For the content between specified levels in the soil, standard names including content_of_soil_layer are used.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0571'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0573/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0573/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0573/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'lwe_thickness_of_water_evaporation_amount'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'lwe\' means liquid water equivalent. \'Amount\' means mass per unit area. The construction lwe_thickness_of_X_amount or _content means the vertical extent of a layer of liquid water having the same mass per unit area. \'Water\' means water in all phases. Evaporation is the conversion of liquid or solid into vapor. (The conversion of solid alone into vapor is called \'sublimation\'.)'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0573'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0574/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0574/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0574/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'land_binary_mask'@en ;
    skos:definition 'X_binary_mask has 1 where condition X is met, 0 elsewhere. 1 = land, 0 = sea.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0574'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0600/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0600/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0600/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'latitude'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Latitude is positive northward; its units of degree_north (or equivalent) indicate this explicitly. In a latitude-longitude system defined with respect to a rotated North Pole, the standard name of grid_latitude should be used instead of latitude. Grid latitude is positive in the grid-northward direction, but its units should be plain degree.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0600'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0601/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0601/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0601/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'leaf_area_index'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'X_area\' means the horizontal area occupied by X within the grid cell.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0601'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0603/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0603/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0603/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'liquid_water_content_of_soil_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. \'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Quantities defined for a soil layer must have a vertical coordinate variable with boundaries indicating the extent of the layer(s).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0603'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0605/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0605/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0605/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'horizontal_atmosphere_dry_energy_transport'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Dry energy is the sum of dry static energy and kinetic energy. Dry static energy is the sum of enthalpy and potential energy (itself the sum of gravitational and centripetal potential energy). Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0605'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0606/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0606/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0606/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'horizontal_dry_energy_transport_in_atmosphere_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Dry energy is the sum of dry static energy and kinetic energy. Dry static energy is the sum of enthalpy and potential energy (itself the sum of gravitational and centripetal potential energy). Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0606'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0607/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0607/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0607/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'humidity_mixing_ratio'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Humidity mixing ratio of a parcel of moist air is the ratio of the mass of water vapor to the mass of dry air.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0607'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0612/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0612/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0612/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'isotropic_longwave_radiance_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'longwave\' means longwave radiation. Radiance is the radiative flux in a particular direction, per unit of solid angle. If radiation is isotropic, the radiance is independent of direction, so the direction should not be specified. If the radiation is directionally dependent, a standard name of upwelling or downwelling radiance should be chosen instead.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0612'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0613/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0613/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0613/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'isotropic_shortwave_radiance_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'shortwave\' means shortwave radiation. Radiance is the radiative flux in a particular direction, per unit of solid angle. If radiation is isotropic, the radiance is independent of direction, so the direction should not be specified. If the radiation is directionally dependent, a standard name of upwelling or downwelling radiance should be chosen instead.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0613'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0615/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0615/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0615/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'kinetic_energy_content_of_atmosphere_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. \'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0615'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0621/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0621/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0621/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'forecast_period'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Forecast period is the time interval between the forecast reference time and the validity time. A period is an interval of time, or the time-period of an oscillation.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0621'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0622/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0622/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0622/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'forecast_reference_time'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The forecast reference time in NWP is the \'data time\', the time of the analysis from which the forecast was made. It is not the time for which the forecast is valid; the standard name of time should be used for that time.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0622'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0623/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0623/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0623/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'fractional_saturation_of_oxygen_in_sea_water'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Fractional saturation is the ratio of some measure of concentration to the saturated value of the same quantity.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0623'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0624/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0624/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0624/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'freezing_level_altitude'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Altitude is the (geometric) height above the geoid, which is the reference geopotential surface. The geoid is similar to mean sea level.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0624'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0626/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0626/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0626/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'frozen_water_content_of_soil_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'frozen_water\' means ice. \'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. \'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Quantities defined for a soil layer must have a vertical coordinate variable with boundaries indicating the extent of the layer(s).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0626'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0627/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0627/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0627/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'geopotential'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Geopotential is the sum of the specific gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the specific centripetal potential energy.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0627'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0628/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0628/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0628/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'geopotential_height'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Geopotential is the sum of the specific gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the specific centripetal potential energy. Geopotential height is the geopotential divided by the standard acceleration due to gravity. It is numerically similar to the altitude (or geometric height) and not to the quantity with standard name height, which is relative to the surface.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0628'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0629/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0629/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0629/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'geopotential_height_anomaly'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'anomaly\' means difference from climatology. Geopotential is the sum of the specific gravitational potential energy relative to the geoid and the specific centripetal potential energy. Geopotential height is the geopotential divided by the standard acceleration due to gravity. It is numerically similar to the altitude (or geometric height) and not to the quantity with standard name height, which is relative to the surface.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0629'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0634/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0634/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0634/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'grid_latitude'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Latitude is positive northward; its units of degree_north (or equivalent) indicate this explicitly. In a latitude-longitude system defined with respect to a rotated North Pole, the standard name of grid_latitude should be used instead of latitude. Grid latitude is positive in the grid-northward direction, but its units should be plain degree.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0634'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0635/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0635/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0635/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'grid_longitude'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Longitude is positive eastward; its units of degree_east (or equivalent) indicate this explicitly. In a latitude-longitude system defined with respect to a rotated North Pole, the standard name of grid_longitude should be used instead of longitude. Grid longitude is positive in the grid-eastward direction, but its units should be plain degree.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0635'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0638/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0638/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0638/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'height'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Height is the vertical distance above the surface.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0638'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0640/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0640/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0640/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'height_at_cloud_top'@en ;
    skos:definition 'cloud_top refers to the top of the highest cloud. Height is the vertical distance above the surface.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0640'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0642/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0642/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0642/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'dry_static_energy_content_of_atmosphere_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. \'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Dry static energy is the sum of enthalpy and potential energy (itself the sum of gravitational and centripetal potential energy). Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0642'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0643/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0643/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0643/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'duration_of_sunshine'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The WMO definition of sunshine is that the surface incident radiative flux from the solar beam (i.e. excluding diffuse skylight) exceeds 120 W m-2. \'Duration\' is the length of time for which a condition holds.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0643'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0644/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0644/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0644/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'eastward_atmosphere_dry_static_energy_transport_across_unit_distance'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Eastward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). Transport across_unit_distance means expressed per unit distance normal to the direction of transport. Dry static energy is the sum of enthalpy and potential energy (itself the sum of gravitational and centripetal potential energy). Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0644'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0645/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0645/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0645/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'eastward_atmosphere_water_transport_across_unit_distance'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Water\' means water in all phases. \'Eastward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). Transport across_unit_distance means expressed per unit distance normal to the direction of transport.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0645'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0646/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0646/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0646/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'eastward_atmosphere_water_vapor_transport_across_unit_distance'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Eastward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). Transport across_unit_distance means expressed per unit distance normal to the direction of transport.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0646'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0647/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0647/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0647/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'eastward_mass_flux_of_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Eastward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0647'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0648/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0648/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0648/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'eastward_momentum_flux_correction'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Eastward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). Momentum flux is dimensionally equivalent to stress and pressure. It is a tensor quantity. Flux correction is also called \'flux adjustment\'. A positive flux correction is downward i.e. added to the ocean. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0648'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0650/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0650/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0650/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'eastward_sea_water_velocity'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A velocity is a vector quantity. \'Eastward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward).'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0650'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0652/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0652/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0652/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'eastward_water_vapor_transport_across_unit_distance_in_atmosphere_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. \'Eastward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). Transport across_unit_distance means expressed per unit distance normal to the direction of transport.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0652'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0653/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0653/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0653/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'eastward_wind'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Eastward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name upward_air_velocity.)'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0653'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0655/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0655/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0655/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'enthalpy_content_of_atmosphere_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. \'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0655'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0656/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0656/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0656/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'equilibrium_line_altitude'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Altitude is the (geometric) height above the geoid, which is the reference geopotential surface. The geoid is similar to mean sea level. The equilibrium line is the locus of points on a land ice surface at which ice accumulation balances ice ablation over the year.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0656'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0658/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0658/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0658/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'equivalent_pressure_of_atmosphere_ozone_content'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. The \'atmosphere content\' of a quantity refers to the vertical integral from the surface to the top of the atmosphere. For the content between specified levels in the atmosphere, standard names including content_of_atmosphere_layer are used. The equivalent pressure of a particular constituent of the atmosphere is the surface pressure exerted by the weight of that constituent alone.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0658'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0671/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0671/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0671/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'dry_energy_content_of_atmosphere_layer'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Content\' indicates a quantity per unit area. \'Layer\' means any layer with upper and lower boundaries that have constant values in some vertical coordinate. There must be a vertical coordinate variable indicating the extent of the layer(s). If the layers are model layers, the vertical coordinate can be model_level_number, but it is recommended to specify a physical coordinate (in a scalar or auxiliary coordinate variable) as well. Dry energy is the sum of dry static energy and kinetic energy. Dry static energy is the sum of enthalpy and potential energy (itself the sum of gravitational and centripetal potential energy). Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0671'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0684/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0684/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0684/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'divergence_of_wind'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'[horizontal_]divergence_of_X\' means [horizontal] divergence of a vector X; if X does not have a vertical component then \'horizontal\' should be omitted. Wind is defined as a two-dimensional (horizontal) air velocity vector, with no vertical component. (Vertical motion in the atmosphere has the standard name upward_air_velocity.)'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0684'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0685/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0685/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0685/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downward_dry_static_energy_flux_due_to_diffusion'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). Dry static energy is the sum of enthalpy and potential energy (itself the sum of gravitational and centripetal potential energy). Enthalpy can be written either as (1) CpT, where Cp is heat capacity at constant pressure, T is absolute temperature, or (2) U+pV, where U is internal energy, p is pressure and V is volume. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0685'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0686/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0686/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0686/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downward_eastward_momentum_flux_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Eastward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed eastward (negative westward). \'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). \'Downward eastward\' indicates the ZX component of a tensor. Momentum flux is dimensionally equivalent to stress and pressure. It is a tensor quantity. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0686'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0688/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0688/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0688/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downward_heat_flux_at_ground_level_in_snow'@en ;
    skos:definition 'ground_level means the land surface (beneath the snow and surface water, if any). \'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0688'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0689/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0689/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0689/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downward_heat_flux_at_ground_level_in_soil'@en ;
    skos:definition 'ground_level means the land surface (beneath the snow and surface water, if any). \'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0689'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0690/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0690/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0690/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downward_heat_flux_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). The vertical heat flux in air is the sum of all heat fluxes i.e. radiative, latent and sensible. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0690'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0692/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0692/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0692/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downward_heat_flux_in_soil'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0692'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0693/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0693/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0693/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downward_northward_momentum_flux_in_air'@en ;
    skos:definition '\'Northward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed northward (negative southward). \'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). \'Downward northward\' indicates the ZY component of a tensor. Momentum flux is dimensionally equivalent to stress and pressure. It is a tensor quantity. In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0693'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0696/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0696/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0696/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'downward_water_vapor_flux_in_air_due_to_diffusion'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The specification of a physical process by the phrase due_to_process means that the quantity named is a single term in a sum of terms which together compose the general quantity named by omitting the phrase. \'Downward\' indicates a vector component which is positive when directed downward (negative upward). In accordance with common usage in geophysical disciplines, \'flux\' implies per unit area, called \'flux density\' in physics.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0696'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0704/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0704/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0704/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'cloud_top_altitude'@en ;
    skos:definition 'cloud_top refers to the top of the highest cloud. Altitude is the (geometric) height above the geoid, which is the reference geopotential surface. The geoid is similar to mean sea level.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0704'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0709/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0709/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0709/>;
    dc:modified '2006-09-26T18:12:43'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'convective_cloud_base_altitude'@en ;
    skos:definition 'cloud_base refers to the base of the lowest cloud. Altitude is the (geometric) height above the geoid, which is the reference geopotential surface. The geoid is similar to mean sea level. Convective cloud is that produced by the convection schemes in an atmosphere model.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P07::CFSN0709'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P07/current/CFSN0710/1/> .
